/* ==========================================================================
   ppe-data.js — PPE Management reference data (Safety Portal)
   ==========================================================================
   Digitized from the official source workbook: PPE_Mangement.xlsx

   REFERENCE DATA extracted verbatim from the real PPE Requirement Matrix,
   PPE/First Aid/Equipment Inventory (opening balances, reorder points, max
   stock), and the workbook's own Dropdown Lists sheet (Issued By,
   Department, Issuance Reason, Item IDs). Loaded as a plain global (no
   build system), matching the rest of this app's architecture.

   Do NOT hand-edit matrix/inventory records here to "fix" something that
   looks unusual — preserve the source data as-is.

   Structure:
     PPE_DATA.issuedBy     — [name]            (master "Issued By" list)
     PPE_DATA.departments  — [name]             (master department list)
     PPE_DATA.reasons      — [name]             (master issuance-reason list)
     PPE_DATA.ppeColumns   — [{col,key,name,group}]  (30 PPE items, grouped)
     PPE_DATA.matrix       — [{task, requirements:{itemKey:'M'|'R'|'-'}}]  (57 tasks/areas)
     PPE_DATA.inventory    — [{id,name,category,unit,opening,received,reorderPoint,maxStock,notes}]
                              (132 items: 47 PPE / 17 First Aid / 68 Equipment)

   Notes:
   - The source workbook's Issuance log (Sheet 3) was a blank template —
     no historical issuance/loss/damage/employee data exists to import.
     Issuance records, stock alerts, and analytics are populated going
     forward from real activity logged through this module, not backfilled
     with invented history.
   - inventory.opening/received are the workbook's starting snapshot;
     Current Stock is always derived at render time (opening + received -
     net issued), never stored as a separate mutable number — see
     ppe.js's stock engine.
   ========================================================================== */
